        "platform": "linux-x86_64",
        "version": "12.4.99"
      },
      "id": "synthetic-stripped-renamed",
      "kind": "synthetic",
      "note": "Generated locally from an already-present corpus library: a COPY that is stripped (symbols/soname removed) and renamed to an innocuous name (e.g. libplugin.so). This defeats name/soname heuristics; only a content hash or build-id survives. Source is resolved from the redist corpus at run time, so nothing is downloaded or committed.",
      "rename_to": "libplugin.so",
      "strip": true,
      "transform": "rename"
    },
    {
      "expect": [
        {
          "component": "cudart",
          "version": "12.4.99"
        }
      ],
      "from_corpus": {
        "component": "cudart",
        "match": "cudart64_12.dll",
        "platform": "windows-x86_64",
        "version": "12.4.99"
      },
      "id": "synthetic-windows-dll-renamed",
      "kind": "synthetic",
      "note": "Windows deployment form: a cudart64_12.dll copied and renamed to an innocuous name (plugin.dll). Exercises the PE/DLL identification path on a renamed binary. Source is the Windows redist already in the corpus.",
      "rename_to": "plugin.dll",
      "transform": "rename"
    },
    {
      "expect": [
        {
          "component": "cudart",
          "version": "12.4.99"
        }
      ],
      "from_corpus": {
        "component": "cudart",
        "match": "libcudart_static.a",
        "platform": "linux-x86_64",
        "version": "12.4.99"
      },
      "id": "synthetic-static-exe",
      "kind": "synthetic",
      "note": "Pure static deployment: the self-contained static runtime libcudart_static.a, which a statically linked app compiles in (no .so at all). cudabom identifies static CUDA by hashing the archive's member objects. The harness links an executable when a matching toolchain exists, else scans the .a directly (the same member-hash path).",
      "transform": "static-exe"
    },
    {
      "expect": [
        {
          "component": "cudart",
          "version": "12.4.99"
        }
      ],
      "from_corpus": {
        "component": "cudart",
        "match": "libcudart.so",
        "platform": "linux-x86_64",
        "version": "12.4.99"
      },
      "id": "synthetic-upx-packed",
      "kind": "synthetic",
      "note": "Adversarial: a CUDA library UPX-compressed. The on-disk bytes change, so a file-hash match is defeated; the finding is whether ANY signal survives (likely a MISS, recorded honestly). Needs upx on PATH; without it the copy is scanned unpacked.",
      "rename_to": "libpacked.so",
      "transform": "upx"
    },
    {
      "expect": [
        {
          "component": "cudart",
          "version": "12.4.99"
        }
      ],
      "from_corpus": {
        "component": "cudart",
        "match": "libcudart.so",
        "platform": "linux-x86_64",
        "version": "12.4.99"
      },
      "id": "synthetic-embedded-blob",
      "kind": "synthetic",
      "note": "Adversarial: a CUDA library concatenated inside a larger blob at a non-zero offset (as a vendored payload embedded in another file would appear). Tests whether the library is identified when it is not the whole file. Resolved by embedded-ELF offset scanning: the library's build-id/symbols identify it at its byte offset even though the whole-file hash matches nothing.",
      "rename_to": "payload.bin",
      "transform": "embed"
    },
